/-! ## (A) THE FREEZE-OUT REMOVAL STAIRCASE — the doubled total of the banked freeze-out steps. -/

/-- THE FREEZE-OUT STAIRCASE CENSUS: the DOUBLED total (both chiralities) of the banked freeze-out
    removal STEPS. Each step is the frozen flavour's derived coloured census term (D2): bottom
    `bandCensus[u,d,s,c,b] − bandCensus[u,d,s,c] = 11/3 − 10/3 = 1/3 = colouredCensusTerm 1`, charm
    `bandCensus[u,d,s,c] − bandCensus[u,d,s] = 10/3 − 2 = 4/3 = colouredCensusTerm 2`. This is the
    coloured content that FREEZES OUT as the scale descends across the quark thresholds. -/
def freezeoutStaircaseCensus : ℚ :=
  2 * ((bandCensus [2, 1, 1, 2, 1] - bandCensus [2, 1, 1, 2])
        + (bandCensus [2, 1, 1, 2] - bandCensus [2, 1, 1]))

/-- THE FREEZE-OUT STAIRCASE CENSUS IS THE DERIVED `10/3`: `2·((11/3−10/3) + (10/3−2)) = 2·(1/3 + 4/3)
    = 2·(5/3) = 10/3` (banked `freezeout_step_bottom`/`freezeout_step_charm` = `colouredCensusTerm
    1`/`2`). The staircase re-supplies the full coloured slice `10/3` across the two chiralities. -/
theorem freezeoutStaircaseCensus_val : freezeoutStaircaseCensus = 10 / 3 := by
  unfold freezeoutStaircaseCensus
  rw [freezeout_step_bottom, freezeout_step_charm, colouredCensusTerm_one, colouredCensusTerm_two]
  norm_num

/-! ## (B) THE STAIRCASE RE-SUPPLIES EXACTLY THE REMOVED COLOURED CONTENT. -/

/-- ★★★ THE FREEZE-OUT STAIRCASE RE-SUPPLIES EXACTLY THE REMOVED COLOURED CONTENT: over the derived ℝ
